Cancel a sign-in waiting for its second factor (tuta-unofficial-sdk)

A sign-in that the user abandons at the second-factor prompt leaves its
session open on the server until it expires. The official client closes it
from SecondFactorAuthDialog through LoginFacade.cancelCreateSession: a
SecondFactorAuthService DELETE naming the pending session, sent without
authentication, since the session cannot authenticate anything before its
second factor is through. The SDK has the generated DELETE binding but no
call that makes it.

Sdk::cancel_second_factor makes it, from the pending session's access token
(parsed as authenticate_with_second_factor_totp parses it), on the same
unauthenticated service executor the other second-factor calls use. Like
TS, it leaves NotFoundError (nothing pending any more) and LockedError (a
code being checked at the same moment) to the caller.

